cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ten-line-transformer
message: >-
  A transformer in one Python file, 123 lines, where one training step is ten
  of them. If you use it in teaching or in a write-up, this is how to cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kwon
    given-names: Youngjune
repository-code: https://github.com/YoungjuneKwon/ten-line-transformer
abstract: >-
  A single-file transformer with training, validation and generation in 123
  lines of PyTorch, written to be read rather than extended. The seed is fixed
  and the loss values are reproducible; every place in the file is mapped line
  by line to the shipping model code of Qwen2.5, Llama and OLMo 2. Built on
  Andrej Karpathy's nanoGPT (MIT) and substantially rewritten.
keywords:
  - transformer
  - language model
  - pytorch
  - from scratch
  - reproducibility
  - teaching
license: MIT
